#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate i18n sidecar translation files for all 49 BP1 process catalogues.

Scope: BP1 + BP2 *names* across 7 target locales (de, es, fr, it, pt, ru, zh).
BP3 (896 nodes), descriptions, aliases, and scope-bullets are deferred to
follow-up PRs to keep the volume of human-quality translations tractable.

Translation strategy:
- One curated translation per source English name per locale (no programmatic
  word-by-word fallback — guarantees grammatical correctness and fluency).
- Noun-form translations are preferred (e.g. "Verwaltung von..." rather than
  imperative "Verwalte ..."), matching the established L1 sidecar style.
- Acronyms (HVAC, BAS, KM, IT, IP, CNS, EHS, GMP, REACH, RBC, IBNR, ORSA,
  SAO, IFRS, S&OP, SaaS, OT, AML, KYC, FNOL, MGA, SIU, SaaS, CX, BAS, PCF,
  BIAN, eTOM, ITIL, SCOR, ACORD, ICMM, ICAO, AS9100) are kept verbatim
  in all locales.
- Industry context preserved: e.g. "Hydrocarbon" → "Kohlenwasserstoff" (de),
  "hidrocarburos" (es); not glossed away.

Output: catalogue/i18n/<locale>/processes/BP1-<slug>.yaml
"""
